<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Release Planning Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Release planning can become challenging when teams work with unclear
                    requirements, changing priorities, incomplete testing, technical
                    dependencies, or unrealistic delivery expectations. A structured
                    approach helps reduce these risks and improve release predictability.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Unclear Release Scope:</b> Establish clear inclusion and exclusion criteria to prevent uncontrolled scope expansion.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Changing Priorities:</b> Maintain a prioritized backlog and evaluate changes based on business and customer impact.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Unrealistic Deadlines:</b> Build timelines based on actual team capacity, dependencies, testing requirements, and delivery complexity.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Incomplete Testing:</b> Define testing activities early and include adequate time for defect resolution and regression testing.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Dependency Issues:</b> Identify dependencies early and assign responsible owners for monitoring them.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Poor Communication:</b> Establish clear communication channels and provide timely release updates to stakeholders.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Insufficient Contingency Planning:</b> Prepare rollback, recovery, and escalation plans for critical release risks.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant challenges image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Release Scope and Prioritization</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Defining and prioritizing release scope helps teams focus on the most
                    valuable product improvements while maintaining realistic delivery
                    expectations. Each release should have a clear purpose and measurable
                    objectives.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Identify the highest-value features and improvements for the release.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Evaluate requirements based on customer impact and business value.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Consider technical complexity, dependencies, resources, and delivery effort.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Separate essential release items from lower-priority enhancements.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Maintain flexibility while protecting critical release objectives.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant scope planning image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Release Timeline and Dependency Management</b></h3>

                <p>
                    A detailed release timeline provides visibility into major milestones,
                    dependencies, testing activities, approvals, and deployment dates.
                    Dependency management helps teams identify potential blockers before
                    they affect the release schedule.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Define development, testing, review, approval, and deployment milestones.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Assign clear ownership for each major release activity.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Track technical and business dependencies throughout the release cycle.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Monitor schedule changes and communicate their impact to stakeholders.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Maintain contingency time for unexpected issues and critical fixes.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant timeline image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
